":"text0","label":"Additional notes","x":-26.526398,"z":-17.652977,"width":17.167822,"height":2.6785185,"rotation":0,"shape":"text"},{"kind":"text","key":"text1","label":"Party should try to stack center of the boss for all Morn Afahs. \nMelees can get their positionals in the center of the hitbox. \nIt also reduces confusion as to where to stack.\nLikewise, tanks should try to take Akh Morn where the boss is already facing. \nThis way, the boss doesn\u0027t spin unexpectedly and the unsafe area is clear.","x":-14.691139,"z":-11.29363,"width":41.34717,"height":7.70449,"rotation":0,"shape":"text"},{"kind":"text","key":"text2","label":"Akh Morn can only ever hit 2 targets maximum. \nThe main tank is guaranteed to be hit,while the 2nd\nperson (if applicable) is any person in range of the tankbuster.","x":-15.600117,"z":-2.917038,"width":38.894436,"height":5.3356085,"rotation":0,"shape":"text"},{"kind":"text","key":"text3","label":"Tanks can opt to tank LB3 a Morn Afah (if 7-man stack/insufficient mit)\nor an Akh Morn (if an invuln is down)","x":-12.986368,"z":3.435732,"width":44.07791,"height":3.413504,"rotation":0,"shape":"text"},{"kind":"text","key":"text4","label":"The enrage Morn Afah (after the 5th) is an AoE around \nthe targeted player that does 2x a person\u0027s HP. \nIf you are seeing this Morn Afah, everybody should \nspread out to try to gain as much time as possible\nto kill the boss. It goes in order of aggro so tanks \ncan opt to shirk healers or players that have died \nin order to allow the people with buffs to live the longest.","x":20.676804,"z":-10.037748,"width":27.887222,"height":10.020873,"rotation":0,"shape":"text"}]}]}